 "defect_1_lookahead_denominator": "pct_circ_now is % of CURRENT (2026-07-24) circulating supply, applied to events back to 2016. Circulating supply GROWS, so an old unlock that was a huge share of float AT THE TIME is recorded as a small share of TODAY's float. The historical >=10% bucket is therefore structurally emptied (insiders >=10%: only 14 events; >=30%: 0), and the conditioning variable is not knowable at event time. The metric is clean PROSPECTIVELY and contaminated historically.",
 "defect_2_snapshot_not_series": "One-shot scrape. Forward calendar spans only 2026-07-25 -> 2026-08-23 (171 events, 45 symbols) and contains ZERO events at >=10% pct_circ_now. No collector refreshes it, so the forward test the mechanism needs cannot be run from this artifact and the file expires 2026-08-23.",
 "verdict": "NOT REFUTED, NOT SUPPORTED -- UNMEASURED at the threshold that carries the mechanism. L1.25: absence of a survivor here is a DATA/INSTRUMENT limitation, not evidence about the market. Loose-threshold cells ARE adequately powered and are a genuine null (|t|<=1.32 vs bars 2.24-2.90).",
 "reentry_condition_L1_16a": "A recurring collector that snapshots the DefiLlama forward calendar so unlocks accrue prospectively, PLUS circulating-supply-at-event-date to replace the contaminated pct_circ_now denominator. Re-test only when >=20 insider events at >=10% of contemporaneous float exist. A new window or threshold on THIS snapshot is NOT an enabling change and would be re-litigating.",
 "bias_direction": "Bronze universe is CURRENTLY-listed perps (survivorship). Survivors outperform, which biases a SHORT study AGAINST finding an edge -- the safe direction."
